      "conf": "SINGLE SOURCE · CAUSE UNCONFIRMED",
      "dek": "The S&P 500 is at 7,701.14, down 0.06%, after being down 0.45% two hours ago. Interest rates did not change their mind: the US 10-year is still 5.11% on the Treasury's own Wednesday table, the last one published. What moved was oil. West Texas crude touched $96.78 this morning and has fallen back to $94.80 on reports that American and Iranian negotiators are discussing lifting the naval blockade on tankers through the Strait of Hormuz — one data vendor's account, which we could not confirm anywhere else. For anyone holding companies for years, the day's story and the day's cause are often different things. Watch whether oil goes back through $96.78.",
