      "conf": "VERIFIED · DATA VENDOR",
      "dek": "The VIX, the market's fear gauge, is at 15.54, up 2.38% on Wednesday's close of 15.18 — but down 0.76 from where it sat two hours ago. That puts it back at the bottom of the band the BuyTrigger ladder calls normal, between 15 and 20, and only 0.54 above the line where the ladder calls the market calm. The ladder's buy window opens at 30, which is 14.46 points above here. In plain terms, nothing today has frightened anyone: an index that gives back half a percent and takes it back is ordinary weather. Watch where it settles at the US close.",
