      "conf": "WIRE REPORTED · NO FILING",
      "dek": "Oracle is at $138.53, down 4.17%, and it touched $133.48 earlier. Almost every other large name on this list has taken back most of its morning loss; Oracle has not. The reason is a report that it sent Blue Owl a force majeure notice over the Project Jupiter data centre in New Mexico, which would let it delay payments if the campus misses its 2028 opening — while it says publicly that the project remains on schedule. We re-checked the SEC's filing database this afternoon: Oracle's newest filing is still dated 23 September and none of them mention this. Until the company files something, this rests on a wire report. Watch for an 8-K.",
