      "conf": "VERIFIED · DATA VENDOR",
      "dek": "Blue Owl Capital, the lender behind the Project Jupiter campus, is at $9.25, down about 3.7%, against Oracle's 4.17% fall — 0.47 of a percentage point apart. That gap matters more than either move. When a tenant runs into trouble you would normally expect its lender to be marked down less, because it sits higher in the queue to be repaid. The market is not making that distinction today: it is pricing the lender almost exactly with the borrower. For a long-term holder, that is the useful signal about how private credit is being valued in this data-centre building boom. Watch whether the gap widens into the close.",
